          "filename": "Carn Liath broch - geograph.org.uk - 60957.jpg",
          "caption": "Carn Liath broch. Carn Liath, the grey cairn, looking anything but grey on a beautiful sunset evening.  It's positioned beside the main road, but secluded, and (as you can see) very close to the sea.  This bit of Sutherland is beautiful!  The broch is reasonably well preserved, with walls up to 12 ft high, and some of the surrounding houses survive.",
